quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  3,149,"O believers! If you yield to the disbelievers, they will turn you back on your heels, and you will turn into losers."
  3,150,"Nay, Allah is your Guardian, and He is the best of helpers."
  3,151,"Soon, We shall cast panic into the hearts of the disbelievers because of their ascribing partners to Allah, for which He has not sent down any authority. And their abode shall be the Fire. How miserable is the abode of the wrongdoers!"
  3,152,"Allah certainly fulfilled His promise to you (at the Battle of Uhud) when you were killing them with His leave, until (the moment) you lost heart, and (some of you) disputed about the matter (of abandoning or sticking to the positions fixed for the archers) and disobeyed (the instructions), after He had shown you (the victory) that you were longing for. Some of you desired the (gains of this) world, and some of you desired the Hereafter. Then He prevented you from (defeating) them so that He might test you. However, He has (now) pardoned you, for Allah is Most Gracious to the believers."
  3,153,"(O believers! Remember) when you were running far away (in a panic) without paying attention to anyone, and the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) was calling you from behind (standing among the group of believers that was steadfast). Then He recompensed you with distress upon distress, so you may not grieve for (the victory) you had lost, nor for (the injury) occurred to you. And Allah is All-Aware of what you do."
